    "gamePaused": "The game is paused.",
    "gameRules": "How to play",
    "gameRulesAllJudgesBody": "In online mode, each person can submit their own complete order. Everyone receives a secret number. Each person takes only as many sips as the errors in their own order. Nobody drinks for someone else’s errors; other people’s orders and results stay private. The current reader can replace the question.",
    "gameRulesAllJudgesTitle": "Everyone is a judge",
    "gameRulesErrorsBody": "Sort people by their answers from the lowest to the highest number. Each position is compared with the complete correct ascending order. Each person in the wrong position counts as one error. Swapping two people means two errors, not one.",
    "gameRulesErrorsTitle": "What counts as an error?",
    "gameRulesExtraRulesBody": "Extra rules appear between cases, apply immediately until the game ends, and do not count as cases. The active drinking rules list shows the rules actually drawn in your game. Each separate violation costs one extra sip, handled manually by the group. No double penalties and no penalty chains. Necessary reading aloud and normal number reveals are exempt from speech restrictions.",
    "gameRulesExtraRulesTitle": "Active drinking rules and violations",
    "gameRulesNextBody": "Normal Next does not ask for errors, sips or people who should drink. With physical cards, the played case is completed without inventing an app score; digital modes keep the automatically calculated verdict. Completing a case without a verdict is a separate interruption action requiring confirmation: it counts the case once but calculates no verdict.",
    "gameRulesNextTitle": "Next and deliberate case interruption",
    "gameRulesNormalBody": "With E errors, the judge takes E sips. Each incorrectly placed person also takes E sips; correctly placed people take none. Example: two wrong positions mean two sips each for the judge and the two incorrectly placed people. With zero errors, nobody drinks because of this verdict.",
    "gameRulesNormalTitle": "Normal verdict and sips",
    "gameRulesRotationBody": "After a completed case, the next person in seating order becomes judge. With physical cards, manage this at the table. Replacing a question stays within the same case: judge, secret numbers, case count and rule schedule remain unchanged. Shown questions are not drawn again in the same game. Once the first digital number is revealed publicly, the question can no longer be replaced.",
    "gameRulesRotationTitle": "Changing judges and questions",
    "gameRulesSetupBody": "Read the question and its scale from 1 to X. Each participant receives a different secret number and gives a matching answer without naming the number. In normal mode the judge has no number. With physical cards, handle numbers and the verdict at the table; in digital modes the app deals and scores.",
    "gameRulesSetupTitle": "Case file and secret numbers",
